cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these numbers, the harness or the workload, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "laya-cuda-bench: Capacity, Tail Latency and Cost of the Laya Decision Models on NVIDIA GPUs"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible capacity-planning benchmark of Laya, Convai's open-weights 421M/322M "System 1" typed-decision
  models, on four NVIDIA GPUs (RTX 2000 Ada Laptop, RTX PRO 5000 Blackwell Laptop, RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell,
  H100 NVL whole and as 7 MIG 1g.12gb slices) with PyTorch eager, torch.compile, ONNX Runtime CUDA and TensorRT.
  It reports sustained decisions per second under p99 latency SLOs of 50 and 130 ms (MLPerf-Server-style
  open-loop sweeps), a 10-million-decision diurnal day replay, cost per million decisions, and baselines against
  a hosted decision API and LLMs (Qwen3.5-35B-A3B-FP8, Qwen3.5-4B) with guided JSON.
authors:
